string.text:
An envoy presents a vassal oath sealed with the royal mark:

[VASSALAGE TREATY]
Suzerain: {SUZERAIN}
Subject: {VASSAL}
Treaty type: {TYPE}
Signed: {DATE}

[BASIC TERMS]
1. The {TYPE} recognizes {SUZERAIN} as suzerain and continues under this treaty identity.
2. The {TYPE} keeps its crown, court, clans, and internal governance; this treaty is not annexation.
{CLAUSES}

The tributary caravan has reached the court. The ledger records:

Subject: {TRIBUTARY}
Recorded: {DATE}
Tribute value: {VALUE}

[SUZERAIN FIEF GAINS]
{GAINS}
[TRIBUTARY COST]
{COST}

Venue: {SETTLEMENT}
Selected guests: {COUNT}.
Choose a clan to open its member list.

Clan: {CLAN}
This is a player-hosted gathering; governors may still be invited. Heroes with independent parties are dispatched directly. Nobles remaining in towns, governors, and heroes without parties travel to the venue using the native system, then return to their original settlement after the gathering.
Selected guests: {COUNT}.

Venue: {SETTLEMENT}
Cost: {COST} denars
Duration: {DAYS} days
Guests: {GUESTS}

Confirming will deduct the cost and send gathering invitations to the guests.

The court scribe has rewritten the vassalage treaty:

Subject: {SUBJECT}
Previous treaty type: {OLD}
New treaty type: {NEW}
Previous signing date: {OLD_DATE}
New signing date: {NEW_DATE}

The old treaty is void: the signing date resets, and the old treaty's tribute records, loyalty, and protection arrangements are archived.

Urgent court dispatch:

Subject: {SUBJECT}
Treaty type: {TYPE}
Signed: {SIGNED}
Ended: {ENDED}
Reason: {REASON}

{MESSAGE}

Border dispatch:

Party breaking the treaty: {DECLARING}
Party declared upon: {TARGET}

{BREAKER} attacked a subject under the suzerain's control, so the tributary treaty has ended.
{SUZERAIN} has automatically protected {TARGET_NAME} and ordered all garrison kingdoms and vassals to join the war against the former tributary.

Border dispatch:

Declaring party: {DECLARING}
Party declared upon: {TARGET}

Both tributaries keep military autonomy. This war is treated as an autonomous war between tributaries: the suzerain will not protect automatically, will not join automatically, and will not dissolve any tributary treaty.
